{"title":"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are five distinct points in space such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fe7a75c754741c8a58c92476d3549a84e397db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB = \\angle BPC = \\angle CPD = \\angle DPA = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"332\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a given acute angle. Determine the greatest and least values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7098b8601ef4893a41abc4f34ae2d960158b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC + \\angle BPD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Greatest value is achieved when all the points are as close as possible to all being on a plane.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b713ceca7cadd92490f6b10f2dd45ddd970fe86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta &lt; \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"34\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b7893eadfc1fb743e55a0f502be28805aa87d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC + \\angle BPD &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Smallest value is achieved when point P is above and the remaining points are as close as possible to colinear when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc6e5e91c929eb11acd83790bdfb01bf794e9f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c0d75a7f00638f8140593072e14054d364f3227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC + \\angle BPD &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>and the inequality for this problem is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f5e231ad376763bde9c3b5f5c5a867574bd244c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\angle APC + \\angle BPD &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"205\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO\" title=\"1984 USAMO\">1984 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174729\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 114/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1617/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2447/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.436      1 -total\n 38.05%    7.776      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 34.28%    7.005      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 26.33%    5.381      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15072:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174729 and revision id 205051. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}